2026-11-01  G. Branden Robinson <g.branden.robinson@gmail.com>

	* src/roff/troff/input.cpp (token::next): Throw warning in
	category "style" if the input uses `\\` to try to format a
	backslash, which is not reliable if the escape character is
	changed (you then get _two_ backslashes instead).  Emit warning
	in category "escape" if encountering an escaped dot.  This
	member function operates only in interpretation mode, so no
	false positives occur when using `\` to escape a dot in copy
	mode, as is sometimes done when nesting macro definitions.

	Fixes <https://savannah.gnu.org/bugs/?68361>.

